  "comments": "There are two unofficial variations, as listed below, which are thought to have been caused by worn punches.<br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">thinner</span> date (at the left) and <span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">lower</span> date (at the right) for 1994<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5d501381d2df4.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5d501381d2df4.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"199\" height=\"53\" /></a><br /><br />\r\nLegends in the 11 Official Languages of the Republic of South Africa:<br />\r\nAfrikaans: Suid-Afrika<br />\r\nEnglish: South Africa<br />\r\nSesotho and Sepedi: Afrika Borwa<br />\r\nTswana: Aforika Borwa<br />\r\nXhosa: uMzantsi Afrika<br />\r\nZulu: iNingizimu Afrika<br />\r\nNdebele: iSewula frika<br />\r\nVenda: Afurika Tshipembe<br />\r\nsiSwati: Ningizimu Afrika<br />\r\nTsonga: Afrika Dzonga",
